<Base lang="en" alt="metodologie/" title="Methodology">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p>Every analysis on the site follows the same rules, so readers can check the conclusions for themselves.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>No figure without a source.</strong> Every dataset has the source’s name, a direct link and the retrieval date. The site cannot be published if any of them is missing.</li>
    <li><strong>Primary sources.</strong> We prefer official institutions (central banks, statistics institutes, the IMF, the World Bank, exchanges) to aggregators.</li>
    <li><strong>Interpretations tied to data.</strong> Every interpretation names the datasets it rests on.</li>
    <li><strong>Transparency about limits.</strong> When data are incomplete or estimated, we say so explicitly.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted">The content is for information only and is not investment advice.</p>
</Base>
